<!--
  Every word the app says, in English.

  Two rules for anyone editing this file:

  1. **The English wording is load-bearing.** The rendering tests in app/src/androidTest assert on
     these exact strings and run under the device's default locale. Changing a word here without
     changing the test that reads it turns a green suite red for a reason that has nothing to do
     with the change.
  2. **Counts go in <plurals>, never in a concatenated string.** English needs two forms; Arabic
     needs six (zero one two few many other). "$n days" cannot be made correct by translation.

  values-ar/strings.xml must carry every key in here — StringResourcesTest fails the build if it
  does not. A missing key does not error at runtime: it silently falls back to English in the
  middle of an Arabic sentence.
-->
